{"entry_id": "2776da28-03e8-48b6-af79-f7587a2ea236", "session_id": "c8c93680-2f90-4fbc-ab76-d57dfb7bc588", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T15:41:13.514163", "query": "A California-based employee with 8 years of service has accumulated 45 days of PTO by\nDecember 31. The Employee Handbook says unused PTO above the carryover cap is forfeited. How much PTO does\nthis employee actually carry into the new year, and why?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "35 days (280 hrs)", "chunk_index": 58}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override", "chunk_index": 4}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 6}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "chunk_index": 8}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees", "chunk_index": 7}], "final_answer": "The employee's unused PTO above the carryover cap will not be forfeited. Instead, they will receive payment at their final rate of pay. Since the employee has 45 days of PTO used by December 31, and California law treats accrued PTO as earned wages, the employee is eligible for payment.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 35 days (280 hrs)\n2. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 1.1 PTO Accrual & Carryover - California Override\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.4 FSA Details - NexCare Plus and Premier Enrollees\n4. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.5 Dependent Care FSA", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
