{"entry_id": "89d01a56-9ea3-4f60-89fe-b4f3f21f008c", "session_id": "87d59462-9702-494d-9e4b-0e9aa1a0cb50", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T15:11:19.993481", "query": "I used the Professional Development Fund to pay for an MBA program this year. If I leave within 18 months, do I have to pay it back?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development", "chunk_index": 63}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions", "chunk_index": 15}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "6.1 Pay Schedule", "chunk_index": 43}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development", "chunk_index": 62}], "final_answer": "If you used the Professional Development Fund to pay for your MBA program and you leave the company voluntarily within 12 months of receiving that funding, you will be subject to a prorated repayment obligation for any amount exceeding $1,000. Since you mentioned the concern about leaving within 18 months, if you leave after the 12-month period, you would not be required to repay the funds. Therefore, if your departure is planned for after 18 months, you should not face any repayment obligations related to the Professional Development Fund. \n\nMake sure to keep track of your timeline and any necessary documentation regarding your funding to ensure compliance with the policy.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 6.1 Pay Schedule", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": false}
{"entry_id": "5de52275-5f16-470e-9b76-67df6ca84016", "session_id": "dfafb5d8-d213-4364-915d-3f79b4f432d7", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T15:20:55.122555", "query": "I used the Professional Development Fund to pay for an MBA program this year. If I leave within 18 months, do I have to pay it back?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "Thought: The user has used the Professional Development Fund for an MBA program, which is not covered under that fund. I need to clarify the repayment obligation related to the Professional Development Fund and confirm the specifics about the MBA program. Since the previous feedback indicated a contradiction regarding the repayment obligation, I will retrieve relevant policy chunks to ensure accurate information.", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development", "chunk_index": 63}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions", "chunk_index": 15}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees", "chunk_index": 5}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "6.1 Pay Schedule", "chunk_index": 43}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development", "chunk_index": 62}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Individual grad school courses", "chunk_index": 31}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "6.1 Annual Wellness Stipend - Eligible Expenses", "chunk_index": 26}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "(PPO+)", "chunk_index": 51}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "NOT COVERED", "chunk_index": 10}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "1.1 Premium Rates - Full Breakdown", "chunk_index": 3}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "6.3 Professional Development Fund - Eligible Use Detail", "chunk_index": 30}, {"document_name": "Nexarion State Policy Addendum", "section_header": "3.3 Chicago Predictive Scheduling (Chicago employees only)", "chunk_index": 22}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "Section 5: Benefits During Leaves of Absence", "chunk_index": 22}], "final_answer": "The Professional Development Fund cannot be used for an MBA program, as degree programs are explicitly excluded from coverage. Since you used the fund for an MBA, this is a violation of the policy. Regarding repayment, if you received funding that exceeded $1,000, you would be obligated to repay that amount if you leave the company within 18 months of receiving the funds. However, since the MBA program is not covered, you should not have received any funding for it through the Professional Development Fund. \n\nTo clarify your situation, you should reach out to HR to discuss the specifics of your case, including any potential repayment obligations and to explore options under the Tuition Reimbursement Program, which may cover degree programs.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.7 Wellness Stipend & Professional Development\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 3.3 Loan and Hardship Withdrawal Provisions\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.3 HSA Details - NexCare Basic Enrollees\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 6.1 Pay Schedule\n5. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Individual grad school courses\n6. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 6.1 Annual Wellness Stipend - Eligible Expenses\n7. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 (PPO+)\n8. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 NOT COVERED\n9. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 1.1 Premium Rates - Full Breakdown\n10. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 6.3 Professional Development Fund - Eligible Use Detail\n11. Nexarion State Policy Addendum \u2014 3.3 Chicago Predictive Scheduling (Chicago employees only)\n12. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 Section 5: Benefits During Leaves of Absence", "grounding_score": 1.0, "compliance_passed": true}
{"entry_id": "56fbeefd-b770-4ec7-9967-edb6fa14322f", "session_id": "02161455-42c2-4531-ab5b-a1b96776e1a1", "user_id": "c2fecc92-8195-47a6-9913-78824671c53e", "timestamp": "2026-04-28T15:50:08.682108", "query": "I want to enroll my dog and my parrot in Nexarion's pet insurance benefit. How do I do that, and what animals are covered?", "route": "hr_in_scope", "escalated": false, "situation_facts": "", "chunks_used": [{"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance", "chunk_index": 53}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "7.3 COBRA Continuation Coverage - Rate Schedule", "chunk_index": 42}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance", "chunk_index": 23}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "7.3 Life & Disability Insurance", "chunk_index": 57}, {"document_name": "Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1)", "section_header": "Section 7: Employee Benefits", "chunk_index": 50}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential", "chunk_index": 25}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential", "chunk_index": 24}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance", "chunk_index": 22}, {"document_name": "Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide", "section_header": "4.1 Company-Provided Coverage Summary", "chunk_index": 20}], "final_answer": "You can enroll your dog in Nexarion's pet insurance benefit, which covers dogs and cats for accident and illness plans. However, your parrot is not covered under this policy, as it only includes dogs and cats. \n\nTo enroll your dog, visit the Nationwide Pet website and complete the enrollment form. The monthly premium for the pet insurance ranges from $28 to $85, depending on the plan you choose and your dog's age and health. Make sure to review the available plans to select one that best fits your needs.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n1. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.1 Health, Dental & Vision Insurance\n2. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 7.3 COBRA Continuation Coverage - Rate Schedule\n3. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.2 Voluntary Supplemental Life Insurance\n4. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 7.3 Life & Disability Insurance\n5. Nexarion Solutions Employee Handbook (1) \u2014 Section 7: Employee Benefits\n6. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 2025 Benefits Guide  |  Confidential\n7. Nexarion 2025 Benefits Guide \u2014 4.1 Company-Provided Coverage Summary", "grounding_score": 0.7, "compliance_passed": true}
